Package: openchronology-server
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Athan Clark <athan.clark@gmail.com>
Section: web
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: postgresql-@PG_MAJOR@, postgresql-common, adduser, libgmp10, libsqlite3-0, ca-certificates
Recommends: systemd
Suggests: nginx | caddy | apache2
Homepage: https://github.com/openchronology/timeline-app
Description: OpenChronology timeline platform server
 The OpenChronology platform: accounts, shared and public timelines, collaboration,
 search and live updates, served by Next.js with PostgreSQL storage. Times are exact
 rationals, stored with the bundled pgmp extension for PostgreSQL @PG_MAJOR@.
 .
 The first installation creates a local PostgreSQL database, migrates it and starts
 the openchronology service on 127.0.0.1:5173. Configuration is in
 /etc/openchronology/openchronology.env. After an upgrade, run openchronology-migrate.
 .
 This package bundles the Node.js @NODE_VERSION@ runtime it is tested with.
